{title: Keep My Commandments}
{subtitle: John 14:15}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] [Bb6] | [Ab] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Whoever believes in me will do [Ab]the works
[Eb]And even greater things than [Ab]these
Because I am [Cm7]going [Bb]to the Fa[Ab]ther [Eb/G]now
What[Ab]ever you ask in my [Bb]name
[Eb]I will do [Bb/D]so the Father is [Ab]glorified
[Eb]In the Son, [Bb/D]I promise [Ab]you
If you ask [Cm7]me a[Bb]nything [Ab]in my [Eb/G]name
[Ab]I will do it, [Bb]trust me now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If you [Eb]love me you will keep [Bb]my command[Ab]ments
And [Eb]I will ask the Fa[Bb]ther for [Ab]you
He will give [Cm7]you another Advo[Bb]cate
I'll ne[Ab]ver for[Eb/G]get to be [Fm7]with [Bb]you, forever [Eb][Bb/D][Cm7]true [Bb6][Ab][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]The Spirit [Bb/D]of truth whom the world [Ab]cannot receive
[Eb]Because it nei[Bb/D]ther sees him [Ab]nor knows him
But you know [Cm7]him for [Bb]he re[Ab]mains with [Eb/G]you
[Ab]And will be in you, [Bb]deep within
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If you [Eb]love me you will keep [Bb]my command[Ab]ments
And [Eb]I will ask the Fa[Bb]ther for [Ab]you
He will give [Cm7]you another Ad[Bb]vo[Ab]cate
To [Eb/G]be with [Fm7]you forever [Eb][Bb/D][Cm7]true [Bb6][Ab][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]I will [Bb/D]not leave [Cm7]you as or[Bb]phans
[Ab]I am coming to you [Bb][Eb][Bb/D]soon
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
